#: ../../source/buffer-fill_readme.md:1
msgid "Buffer Fill"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/buffer-fill_readme.md:3
msgid "A [ponyfill](https://ponyfill.com) for `Buffer.fill`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/buffer-fill_readme.md:5
msgid "Works as Node.js: `v6.4.0` <br> Works on Node.js: `v0.10.0`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/buffer-fill_readme.md:8
msgid "Installation"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/buffer-fill_readme.md:14
msgid "Usage"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/buffer-fill_readme.md:33
msgid "API"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/buffer-fill_readme.md:35
msgid "fill(buf, value[, offset[, end]][, encoding])"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/buffer-fill_readme.md:37
msgid ""
"`value` &lt;String&gt; | &lt;Buffer&gt; | &lt;Integer&gt; The value to "
"fill `buf` with"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/buffer-fill_readme.md:38
msgid "`offset` &lt;Integer&gt; Where to start filling `buf`. **Default:** `0`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/buffer-fill_readme.md:39
msgid ""
"`end` &lt;Integer&gt; Where to stop filling `buf` (not inclusive). "
"**Default:** `buf.length`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/buffer-fill_readme.md:40
msgid ""
"`encoding` &lt;String&gt; If `value` is a string, this is its encoding. "
"**Default:** `'utf8'`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/buffer-fill_readme.md:41
msgid "Return: &lt;Buffer&gt; A reference to `buf`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/buffer-fill_readme.md:43
msgid ""
"Fills `buf` with the specified `value`. If the `offset` and `end` are not"
" given, the entire `buf` will be filled. This is meant to be a small "
"simplification to allow the creation and filling of a `Buffer` to be done"
" on a single line."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/buffer-fill_readme.md:47
msgid ""
"If the final write of a `fill()` operation falls on a multi-byte "
"character, then only the first bytes of that character that fit into "
"`buf` are written."
msgstr ""

